# oracle: fix nph/body with independent x and y barostats (target pressure 0.1, no couple) and pair body/rounded/polygon on the 2x2 squares of examples/body/in.squares, 500 steps, no thermostat (the example uses npt/body with a thermostat). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 4.9e-12 (pxy, step 500); past about step 550 a contact choice flips in this symmetric lattice and the runs separate, as in w126body_squares_npt_xy.
# oracle-inputs: w111body_squares.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      body rounded/polygon 1 6
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w111body_squares.data
replicate       2 2 1
velocity        all create 0.5 980411 dist gaussian mom yes rot yes
pair_style      body/rounded/polygon 1 1 0.1 0.5 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 2
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nph/body x 0.1 0.1 1.0 y 0.1 0.1 1.0 fixedpoint 0 0 0
fix             2 all enforce2d
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pxy
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          100
run             500
